$y$-axis at $y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/9c77bec4ebb04668fbff5176418ed9c09143a8660879fdf523a158c5f109006c.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a maximum at $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-27009/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-27009"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a267687e-58eb-59e7-a5c6-b443c6adc495" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c9fae0d0-3a6c-5972-9f42-618a98a872b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "48a5881f-1ef0-5fd2-bc52-2aafb1b96225" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "7f122c9a-5bdf-5d6d-8cd0-9befb2cff6df" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "fc4c251b-aebe-53c1-b5d6-4eb73fc0a201" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d3c8bff-afb2-59b8-b988-98dfec6ec33d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70666/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-70666/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-70666/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-70666/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-70666/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-70666/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70666" :question/id #uuid "c8200e68-ad7d-55ad-afa5-1d575a43e94f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70666" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$\n- The function is zero at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70666/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7"] :knowledge-point/ques