r any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=\\frac{1}{2},$ then $cos⁡(x-10\\pi )=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70671/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c25c3a0-083a-55d5-b688-7347bfafaa9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "2cb420bb-3d63-53ba-9980-bc74ae6cb5a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3dc323c8-b9be-5eb9-b6a6-5f1ce08e50e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" :answer/id #uuid "86d5b574-a6ee-51d9-95dd-60707d4c5b16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection/cd7e58376862dfa407ef027ba77235975e9e80d4832fcaa8aaa30bc3178da6a5" :answer/id #uuid "73e4ee61-8b56-5633-a858-b76c9d0bced6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0ff8e757-364d-519c-91f1-f3aa988ad5ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a4f6c9-a608-5d09-af9c-db72e6bf71d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-158059/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-158059/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-158059/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-158059/selection/d0ab94490dee12664d2f70471811316d5faf74c9c2c3f6dde546976ea292b76b" "q-158059/selection/cd7e58376862dfa407ef027ba77235975e9e80d4832fcaa8aaa30bc3178da6a5" "q-158059/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-158059" :question/id #uuid "f3a9e284-20ad-5ca4-9756-497c45717d6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-158059" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=0,$ then $\\pi cos⁡(-x+18\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13933487/assets/2373daf4b5fd26f098bf90e998e2685db6a8b793e94ac9d80b08ea423cb535c0.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric over the $y$-axis. This means that $cos⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡(-x)=cos⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $cos⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡(-x+18\\pi ) & =cos⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 9) \\\\  & =cos⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $cos⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡(-x) & =cos⁡x \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi cos⁡(-x+18\\pi )-\\frac{1}{2} & =\\pi \\cdot 0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-158059/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94645507-186a-54a7-a96b-ccfb0fb1f769"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-158059"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-158047/selection/8a135ace4937b1ffa2c52fbce040999428005f5